#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:2
msgid "CMake 4.5 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:5
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:8
msgid "Changes made since CMake 4.4 include the following."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:11
msgid "New Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:14
msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:16
msgid ""
"The :diagnostic:`CMD_NON_TARGET_DIRECTIVE` diagnostic category was added to "
"diagnose commands that affect the directory scope when comparable target-"
"specific commands exist. The use of such directives is discouraged. This "
"diagnostic may be controlled with the :option:`-Wnon-target-directive <cmake "
"-W>` command-line option, the ``nonTargetDirective`` field in a :manual:"
"`CMake Presets <cmake-presets(7)>` :preset:`configurePresets.warnings` "
"object, or the :command:`cmake_diagnostic` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:26
msgid ""
"The :diagnostic:`CMD_STRICT` diagnostic category was added to control "
"diagnostics regarding allowed but discouraged usage as a group. This "
"diagnostic may be controlled with the :option:`-Wstrict <cmake -W>` command-"
"line option, the ``strict`` field in a :manual:`CMake Presets <cmake-"
"presets(7)>` :preset:`configurePresets.warnings` object, or the :command:"
"`cmake_diagnostic` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:35
msgid "Presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:37
msgid ":manual:`cmake-presets(7)` files now support schema version 13."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:39
msgid ""
":manual:`cmake-presets(7)` gained the ``${configurePresetName}`` macro to "
"expand to the name of the configure preset associated with the preset being "
"evaluated. It is available for configure, build, test, and package presets, "
"but not for workflow presets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:45
msgid "File-Based API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:47
msgid ""
"The :manual:`cmake-file-api(7)` \"codemodel\" version 2 ``version`` field "
"has been updated to 2.12."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:50
msgid ""
"The :manual:`cmake-file-api(7)` \"codemodel\" version 2 \"target\" object "
"gained a new ``interfaceIncludes`` array field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:54
msgid "Instrumentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:56
msgid ""
"The :manual:`cmake-instrumentation(7)` data version has been updated to 1.2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:58
msgid ""
":manual:`cmake-instrumentation(7)` now records an overall ``cmakeBuild`` "
"snippet even when a :option:`cmake --build` invocation is interrupted by the "
"user (for example with Ctrl+C).  The snippet includes a new "
"``interruptSignal`` field, recording the signal that interrupted the build, "
"so that consumers can distinguish an interrupted build from one that ran to "
"completion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:65
msgid ""
":manual:`cmake-instrumentation(7)` now records an overall ``cmakeInstall`` "
"snippet, marked with the same ``interruptSignal`` field, when a :option:"
"`cmake --install` invocation is interrupted by the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:69
msgid ""
":manual:`cmake-instrumentation(7)` now records an overall ``ctest`` snippet, "
"marked with the same ``interruptSignal`` field, when a :manual:`ctest(1)` "
"invocation is interrupted by the user.  On interrupt CTest stops scheduling "
"further tests and preserves its checkpoint file so that a later :option:"
"`ctest -F` can resume the interrupted test set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:76
msgid "Generators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:78
msgid ""
"The :ref:`Ninja Generators`, :ref:`Makefile Generators`, and :generator:"
"`FASTBuild` generator now provide ``install_prep/all`` and ``install_prep/"
"<component>`` convenience build targets by default.  The :variable:"
"`CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_PREP_TARGETS` variable may be enabled to skip generating "
"them.  These targets build all known build dependencies for an installation "
"that does not select a component, or for the named install component, "
"respectively.  This includes targets that produce installed C++ module BMIs, "
"module export metadata, or generated files.  See :ref:`Install Preparation "
"Targets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:88
msgid ""
"The :generator:`FASTBuild` generator and the :ref:`Makefile Generators` now "
"provide ``test_prep/<test-name>`` and ``test_prep/all`` convenience build "
"targets by default.  The :variable:`CMAKE_SKIP_TEST_PREP_TARGETS` variable "
"may be enabled to skip generating them.  These targets build the "
"dependencies of tests added by :command:`add_test`, including those listed "
"with the ``BUILD_DEPENDS`` keyword.  See :ref:`Test Preparation Targets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:95
msgid ""
"The :ref:`Ninja Generators` now provide ``test_prep/<test-name>`` and "
"``test_prep/all`` convenience build targets build targets by default.  The :"
"variable:`CMAKE_SKIP_TEST_PREP_TARGETS` variable may be enabled to skip "
"generating them.  These targets were previously generated only if :variable:"
"`CMAKE_TEST_BUILD_DEPENDS` was enabled.  See :ref:`Test Preparation Targets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:102
msgid ""
":ref:`Makefile Generators` and :ref:`Ninja Generators` gained support for "
"adding a linker launcher with ``CUDA`` and ``HIP``. See the :variable:"
"`CMAKE_<LANG>_LINKER_LAUNCHER` variable and :prop_tgt:"
"`<LANG>_LINKER_LAUNCHER` target property for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:108
msgid "Languages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:110
msgid ""
"``import std`` is now available for all C++ 20 and later code with :prop_tgt:"
"`CXX_SCAN_FOR_MODULES` enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:114
msgid "Compilers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:116
msgid ""
"The `open-source DPC++ compiler`_, version 7.0 and newer, is now supported "
"with :variable:`compiler id <CMAKE_<LANG>_COMPILER_ID>` ``DPClang`` for "
"languages ``C`` and ``CXX``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:123
msgid "Command-Line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:125
msgid ""
"The :option:`cmake -E capabilities <cmake-E capabilities>` output now "
"includes an ``instrumentation`` object reporting the supported "
"instrumentation API version and the latest supported data version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:129
msgid ""
"The :option:`cmake --list-presets <cmake --list-presets>` option gained ``*-"
"defined`` values that list all non-hidden presets of the corresponding type "
"and explain why unavailable presets cannot be used. The ``defined`` value is "
"an alias for ``configure-defined``, while ``all-defined`` selects every "
"type. Build, test, and package presets whose configure preset is unavailable "
"are now considered unavailable too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:136
msgid ""
"The :option:`cmake --build --list-presets=defined <cmake--build --list-"
"presets>`, :option:`ctest --list-presets=defined <ctest --list-presets>`, "
"and :option:`cpack --list-presets=defined <cpack --list-presets>` options "
"were added to list all defined build, test, and package presets, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:142
msgid ""
"The :option:`cmake --workflow --list-presets=defined <cmake--workflow --list-"
"presets>` option was added to provide the same availability information for "
"all defined workflow presets and their steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:147
msgid "Commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:149
msgid ""
"The :command:`add_custom_rule` command was added to allow the definition of "
"pattern rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:152
msgid ""
"The :command:`add_dependencies` command now accepts :ref:`Alias Targets`. "
"Dependencies are added to the target the alias references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:155
msgid ""
"The :command:`discover_tests` command gained a ``BUILD_DEPENDS`` argument to "
"support the :ctest-option:`--out-of-date` behavior of :manual:`ctest(1)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:158
msgid ""
"The :command:`cmake_language(PRINT_PROPERTIES)` command was added to print "
"CMake entities' properties in human-readable form for debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:162
msgid ""
"The :command:`cmake_language(PRINT_TARGETS)` command was added to print the "
"targets that currently exist in human-readable form for debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:166
msgid ""
"The :command:`cmake_language(PRINT_VARIABLES)` command was added to print "
"variables and their values in human-readable form for debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:170
msgid ""
"The :command:`file(ARCHIVE_CREATE)` command gained a ``PATTERNS_EXCLUDE`` "
"option to omit files and directories matching the given patterns from the "
"created archive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:174
msgid ""
"The :command:`file(ARCHIVE_EXTRACT)` command gained a ``PATTERNS_EXCLUDE`` "
"option to omit archive entries matching the given patterns from being "
"extracted or listed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:178
msgid ""
"The :command:`file(GET_RUNTIME_DEPENDENCIES)` command is now implemented on "
"FreeBSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:181
msgid ""
"The :command:`find_package` command now supports importing |CPS|_ "
"`executable` components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:184
msgid ""
"The :command:`function` command now sets the ``ARGNC`` variable, which holds "
"the number of arguments past the last expected argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:187
msgid ""
"The :command:`if` command gained a ``PATH_IS_PREFIX`` operator to test "
"whether one path is a prefix of another without accessing the filesystem. "
"See policy :policy:`CMP0222`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:191
msgid ""
"The :command:`if` command gained a ``RULE`` operator to check if a rule "
"exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:194
msgid ""
"The :command:`install` and :command:`export` commands now accept :ref:`Alias "
"Targets`.  The commands operate on the underlying aliased target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:198
msgid ""
"The :command:`install(SBOM)` and :command:`export(SBOM)` commands were added "
"to generate Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:201
msgid ""
"The :command:`install(TARGETS)` command no longer requires a ``LIBRARY "
"DESTINATION`` for :ref:`Module Libraries`.  When no destination is given, a "
"module library is installed to the default ``RUNTIME`` destination on DLL "
"platforms and to the default ``LIBRARY`` destination on other platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:207
msgid ""
"The :command:`install(TARGETS)` command gained a "
"``RUNTIME_DEPENDENCY_TARGETS`` option to install runtime artifacts of non-"
"imported shared libraries from the same build that the named targets link "
"to.  Unlike ``RUNTIME_DEPENDENCIES``, this uses CMake target graph "
"information rather than :command:`file(GET_RUNTIME_DEPENDENCIES)`. The "
"option cannot be used with ``EXPORT`` and may only install runtime artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:215
msgid ""
"The :command:`install` command's ``FILES``, ``PROGRAMS``, ``DIRECTORY``, "
"``SCRIPT``, and ``CODE`` signatures gained a ``BUILD_DEPENDS`` option to "
"specify targets or files needed to prepare files or run installation code.  "
"See :ref:`Install Preparation Targets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:220
msgid ""
"The :command:`math` command gained new ``INCREMENT`` and ``DECREMENT`` modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:222
msgid ""
"The :command:`project` and :command:`enable_language` commands, when called "
"in subdirectories, now propagate support for enabled languages to all "
"ancestor scopes up to the top-level directory, including through enclosing :"
"command:`block` and :command:`function` scopes. See policy :policy:`CMP0220`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:228
msgid ""
"The :command:`set_property` and :command:`get_property` commands now "
"support :ref:`RULE properties <Rule Properties>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:231
msgid ""
"The :command:`set_property` and :command:`set_target_properties` commands "
"now accept :ref:`Alias Targets`. Properties are set on the target which the "
"alias references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:235
msgid ""
"The :command:`string(JSON)` command gained an ``ARRAY_SPLIT`` mode that "
"splits a JSON array into a list of its elements with a single parse, "
"enabling linear-time array iteration instead of re-parsing the whole JSON "
"string for each element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:240
msgid ""
"The :command:`target_compile_definitions`, :command:"
"`target_compile_features`, :command:`target_compile_options`, :command:"
"`target_include_directories`, :command:`target_link_directories`, :command:"
"`target_link_libraries`, :command:`target_link_options`, :command:"
"`target_precompile_headers`, and :command:`target_sources` commands now "
"accept :ref:`Alias Targets`. The command operates on the target the alias "
"references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:248
msgid "File Sets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:250
msgid ""
"|CPS|_ import by :command:`find_package`, and export by :command:"
"`install(PACKAGE_INFO)` and :command:`export(PACKAGE_INFO)`, now support "
"header file sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:254
msgid "The :command:`source_group` command gained support for file sets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:256
msgid ""
"The :prop_tgt:`FILE_SET_TYPES`, :prop_tgt:`FILE_SETS_<TYPE>`, and :prop_tgt:"
"`INTERFACE_FILE_SETS_<TYPE>` target properties were added to get information "
"about file sets attached to the target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:260
msgid ""
"The :prop_fs:`LANGUAGE` file set property was added to select the compile "
"language for members of a ``SOURCES`` file set without modifying their :"
"prop_sf:`LANGUAGE` source file property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:264
msgid ""
"The :prop_fs:`SOURCE_GROUP` file set property and :prop_sf:`SOURCE_GROUP` "
"source file property were added to provide a fine grain control over the "
"grouping of sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:269
msgid "Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:271
msgid ""
"The :variable:`CMAKE_CXX_STDLIB_MODULES_JSON` variable was added to set the "
"path to the ``import std`` metadata file for the standard library rather "
"than using the compiler to discover its location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:275
msgid ""
"The :variable:`CMAKE_INSTALL_SBOM_FORMATS` variable was added to enable "
"Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:278
msgid ""
"The :variable:`CMAKE_TEST_BUILD_DEPENDS` variable is no longer honored. Test "
"preparation targets are now enabled by default.  The :variable:"
"`CMAKE_SKIP_TEST_PREP_TARGETS` variable may be enabled to skip generating "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:284
msgid "Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:286
msgid ""
"The :envvar:`CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ID` environment variable was added to "
"hint to :manual:`cmake(1)` when :cmake-option:`--fresh` may be necessary, "
"along with :envvar:`CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ACTION` to control what happens "
"when :envvar:`CMAKE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_ID` changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:292
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:294
msgid ""
"The :prop_gbl:`CMAKE_COMPILE_WRAPPER_<NAME>` and :prop_gbl:"
"`CMAKE_LINK_WRAPPER_<NAME>` global properties were added alongside the :"
"prop_tgt:`COMPILE_WRAPPERS`, :prop_tgt:`LINK_WRAPPERS`, :prop_tgt:"
"`INTERFACE_COMPILE_WRAPPERS`, and :prop_tgt:`INTERFACE_LINK_WRAPPERS` target "
"properties. Together, for the :ref:`Makefile Generators` and :ref:`Ninja "
"Generators`, they support wrapping compile and link commands for a given "
"target or its consumers with arbitrary command lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:303
msgid ""
"The :prop_dir:`CMAKE_TEST_BUILD_DEPENDS` directory property was added to "
"support directory-scoped build time dependencies for tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:306
msgid ""
"The :prop_tgt:`Fortran_BUILDING_INTRINSIC_MODULES` target property is now "
"honored by the :ref:`Ninja Generators`.  Previously it was only honored by "
"the :ref:`Makefile Generators`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:310
msgid ""
"The :prop_tgt:`Swift_MODULE_NAME` target property is now honored by the :"
"generator:`Xcode` generator.  See policy :policy:`CMP0226`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:313
msgid ""
"The :prop_dir:`TEST_INCLUDE_FILES` and :prop_dir:`TEST_INCLUDE_FILE` "
"directory properties now support :manual:`generator expressions <cmake-"
"generator-expressions(7)>` in the include path.  On multi-config generators "
"a ``$<CONFIG>``-parameterized path can select a different script per "
"configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:319
msgid ""
"The :prop_tgt:`XCODE_EMBED_<type>` target property now supports :manual:"
"`generator expressions <cmake-generator-expressions(7)>`. Because Xcode "
"shares one copy-files build phase across all configurations, an expression "
"whose result depends on the configuration is rejected with an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:326
msgid "Modules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:328
msgid ""
"The :module:`ExternalProject` module's :command:`ExternalProject_Add` "
"command now sets :variable:`CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX` to the external project's "
"``INSTALL_DIR`` in its default configure command, so a CMake external "
"project installs into the prefix the module reserves for it rather than the "
"built-in default (e.g. ``/usr/local``). A caller-supplied prefix still takes "
"precedence. See policy :policy:`CMP0225`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:336
msgid ""
"The :module:`FindCUDAToolkit` module now creates ``CUDAToolkit::`` namespace "
"targets and changes the existing ``CUDA::`` namespace targets to be alias "
"targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:340
msgid ""
"The :module:`FindDoxygen` module :command:`doxygen_add_docs` command gained "
"a ``USES_TERMINAL`` option to give the Doxygen command direct access to the "
"terminal during the build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:344
msgid ""
"The :module:`FindPython`, :module:`FindPython2`, and :module:`FindPython3` "
"modules gained the possibility to override the :variable:"
"`CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR` variable by respectively, the variables "
"``Python_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR``, ``Python2_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR``, and "
"``Python3_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:350
msgid ""
"The :module:`FindPython3` and :module:`FindPython` modules gained, "
"respectively, the variable ``Python3_SOSABI_PLATFORM`` and "
"``Python_SOSABI_PLATFORM`` which gives, on some platforms, for the Stable "
"Application Binary Interface, the extension including the platform triplet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:356
msgid "Generator Expressions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:358
msgid ""
"The :genex:`$<ARGS>` generator expression was added to convert a :ref:"
"`semicolon-separated list <CMake Language Lists>` into a comma-separated "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:362
msgid ""
"The :genex:`$<DIRECTORY_PROPERTY>` generator expression was added to query "
"directory properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:365
msgid ""
"The :genex:`$<GLOBAL_PROPERTY>` generator expression was added to query "
"global properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:368
msgid ""
"The :genex:`LIST` generator expression's ``FILTER`` and ``TRANSFORM`` "
"operations gained a ``PREDICATE`` keyword that selects items by evaluating "
"an arbitrary generator expression once per item, with ``$<_0>`` referring to "
"the current item.  ``FILTER`` also gained an explicit ``REGEX`` keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:373
msgid ""
"The :genex:`LIST` generator expression's ``SORT`` operation gained a "
"``COMPARATOR`` option that orders items using an arbitrary generator "
"expression evaluated once per comparison, with ``$<_0>`` and ``$<_1>`` "
"referring to the two items being compared."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:378
msgid ""
"The :genex:`LIST` generator expression's ``TRANSFORM`` operation gained an "
"``APPLY`` action that evaluates an arbitrary generator expression for each "
"element, with ``$<_0>`` referring to the current element."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:382
msgid ""
"The :genex:`$<LINK_LIBRARY:NEEDED_LIBRARY,...>` generator expression feature "
"is now supported on Linux with GNU-compatible linkers (GNU ld, gold, LLD, "
"MOLD)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:386
msgid ""
"The :genex:`RULE_PROPERTY` generator expression was added to query "
"properties of rules created by the :command:`add_custom_rule` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:390
msgid "Autogen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:392
msgid ""
":prop_tgt:`AUTOMOC` now processes C++ module interface and partition units "
"that are members of a ``FILE_SET`` of type ``CXX_MODULES``. ``moc`` is run "
"on such units and its generated output is compiled as a module "
"implementation unit of the same module.  This requires Qt 6.13 or newer, "
"whose ``moc`` supports C++ module units."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:398
msgid ""
":prop_tgt:`AUTOMOC` now has its generated ``mocs_compilation.cpp`` scanned "
"for C++ module dependencies under the same conditions as the target's own "
"sources.  A header that imports a module may now be processed by ``moc``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:404
msgid "CTest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:406
msgid ""
":manual:`ctest(1)` gained a :ctest-option:`--out-of-date` option to run only "
"tests whose recorded build dependencies are newer than the last time the "
"tests ran."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:410
msgid ""
":manual:`ctest(1)` now supports :ref:`job server integration <ctest-job-"
"server-integration>` on Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:413
msgid ""
"The :manual:`ctest(1)` :ctest-option:`--show-only` option gained a ``json-v1-"
"raw`` format in which the ``value`` for each test property is the original "
"unparsed string value specified in CMake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:417
msgid ""
"The :command:`ctest_test` and :command:`ctest_memcheck` commands gained the "
"ability to accept more than one value for their ``INCLUDE_LABEL`` and "
"``EXCLUDE_LABEL`` options.  When multiple regular expressions are given, a "
"test is selected only if each expression matches at least one of the test's "
"labels (i.e. the expressions form an ``AND`` relationship), matching the "
"behavior of repeating the :option:`ctest --label-regex` and :option:`ctest --"
"label-exclude` command-line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:425
msgid ""
"The :prop_test:`GENERATED_RESOURCE_SPEC_FILE` test property gained support "
"for relative paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:428
msgid ""
"The :prop_test:`FIXTURE_REPEAT_MODE` test property was added to select how a "
"test fixture behaves when :manual:`ctest(1)` repeats tests with its :ctest-"
"option:`--repeat` option.  See policy :policy:`CMP0224`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:432
msgid ""
"The :prop_test:`RESOURCE_ERROR_ACTION` test property and :variable:"
"`CTEST_RESOURCE_ERROR_ACTION` variable were added to configure the test "
"behavior in case of insufficient resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:437
msgid "CPack"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:439
msgid ""
"The :cpack_gen:`CPack APK Generator` was added to package Android "
"applications as APK files.  It drives the Android SDK build tools directly "
"and does not require Gradle.  Maven dependencies, such as the AndroidX "
"libraries, can be downloaded with :variable:`CPACK_APK_MAVEN_DEPENDENCIES`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:446
msgid "Deprecated and Removed Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:448
msgid "The :generator:`Visual Studio 14 2015` generator has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:450
msgid ""
"The :module:`CMakePrintHelpers` module's :command:`cmake_print_properties` "
"command is now deprecated in favor of :command:"
"`cmake_language(PRINT_PROPERTIES)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:454
msgid ""
"The :module:`CMakePrintHelpers` module's :command:`cmake_print_variables` "
"command is now deprecated in favor of :command:"
"`cmake_language(PRINT_VARIABLES)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:458
msgid ""
"The :command:`install_files`, :command:`install_programs`, :command:"
"`install_targets`, :command:`make_directory`, :command:`remove`, :command:"
"`subdirs` and :command:`write_file` commands, which have been deprecated "
"since CMake 3.0, now emit deprecation diagnostics when used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:464
msgid "Other Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:466
msgid ""
"The :option:`cmake --build` command now groups the output of each recipe in "
"a parallel build so that concurrent jobs do not interleave, when CMake is "
"the one passing the parallel flag to the build tool (via :option:`--parallel "
"<cmake--build --parallel>` or :envvar:`CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL`) and that "
"tool is GNU Make 4.0 or newer.  Request parallelism natively, e.g. ``cmake --"
"build . -- -j``, to opt out and stream output as it is produced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:473
msgid ""
"The :option:`cmake --install` command now reports a non-zero exit code when "
"an install script fails.  Previously, a parallel install (enabled by the :"
"prop_gbl:`INSTALL_PARALLEL` global property) always reported success, and a "
"serial install could lose the failure of an earlier component that exited "
"via :command:`cmake_language(EXIT) <cmake_language>` when a later component "
"succeeded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:480
msgid ""
"The :command:`cmake_host_system_information` command's ``DISTRIB_*`` queries "
"now read the host os-release by default.  See policy :policy:`CMP0221`. A "
"new ``FROM_SYSROOT <bool>`` option explicitly enables or disables reading "
"the target os-release from :variable:`CMAKE_SYSROOT`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:485
msgid ""
"The :command:`cmake_path(IS_PREFIX)` command and the :genex:`$<PATH:"
"IS_PREFIX>` generator expression no longer treat an empty path as a prefix "
"of every path.  The :command:`if` command's ``PATH_IS_PREFIX`` operator "
"follows the same rule. See policy :policy:`CMP0223`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:491
msgid ""
"When CTest build launchers are enabled (see the :module:`CTestUseLaunchers` "
"module), a build rule that is terminated by a signal is now reported as a "
"build failure.  Previously such a rule was reported as success, so a crashed "
"compiler, linker, or custom command could be recorded as a passing build on "
"the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:497
msgid "The :prop_tgt:`ALIASED_TARGET` target property is now read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:499
msgid ""
"The Qt Help (``.qch``) rendition of the documentation now carries its own "
"color scheme.  Previously it was rendered with layout rules only, because "
"the ``qthelp`` builder does not generate the color scheme that the HTML "
"documentation uses.  A dark variant is shipped alongside it, which help "
"viewers such as Qt Creator use when their own theme is dark."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release/4.5.rst:505
msgid ""
"The precompiled macOS binary provided on ``cmake.org`` now requires macOS 11 "
"or newer for command-line tools.  The :manual:`cmake-gui(1)` application "
"still requires macOS 12."
msgstr ""
